## 5. RISK ASSESSMENT

| Fix | Blast Radius | Reversibility | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Phase 1** (instrument) | Zero — pure logging | Trivial | None. Highest-value first step. |
| **Phase 2** (compute ATR) | Medium — ATR feeds SL buffers, zone thickness, LQZ. Wrong ATR will shift SL distances across all setups | Medium — add step, don't replace existing if present | Medium. Verify no existing ATR source is being shadowed. Compare pre/post `sl_distance_pips` in setups. |
| **Phase 3** (key normalization) | High — touches every pair-keyed map in the codebase (zones, spots, atr, bars, setups) | Low once normalized; high if done ad hoc | High if done as a one-off string replace. **Mitigation:** centralize via `normalizePairKey()` and grep all `[pair]` accesses. |
| **Phase 4** (loud returns) | Low — only adds logs | Trivial | None. Defense in depth. |
| **Phase 5** (loosen filters) | Low — only affects LQZ output volume | Easy | Low. Only pursue if Phase 1 confirms this is the layer. |

**Critical interaction risk:** Phase 2 changes ATR for *all consumers*, not just LQZ. Per `V3.2_BUILD_REPORT_AND_DEBUG_LOG.md:17` ("ZFP Computation Fix"), the ZFP computation already had a propagation bug fixed once. ATR changes may interact with ZFP via pressure-degree mapping (`SYNTHESIS/02_ENGINE3_V8_PORTING_GUIDE.md` PressureDegree enum). Run the full integration test (`test-report.ts`) before and after, and diff: zone count, setup count, `passedFirewall`, average `sl_distance_pips`. If `sl_distance_pips` distribution shifts materially, ATR is now feeding SL sizing differently — investigate before shipping.

**Test-masking risk (per Evidence E6):** The 18/18 smoke tests will continue to pass regardless of which fix is applied, because they bypass the pipeline. **Do not treat smoke tests as regression coverage for this fix.** Add a new integration assertion (see Phase 6).

