## 7. SUMMARY (One-paragraph root cause)

LQZ produces zero zones because its required input `pairATR` is never populated in the pipeline (Evidence E3: `pairATR: not computed`), even though the raw 1H bars exist (Evidence E4: 500 bars). The LQZ function, finding no ATR, silently returns `[]` (or is guarded out before being called), producing zero zones (Evidence E5: identical counts) and zero logs (Evidence E2: no LQZ diagnostic output). The 18/18 smoke tests pass because they inject ATR directly into the function, bypassing the broken pipeline dataflow (Evidence E6). The fix is not in the LQZ function — it is upstream, in the ATR computation step that populates `zoneMap.atr[pair]`. Instrument first (Phase 1) to confirm the exact failure mode, then repair the ATR step (Phase 2) or the pair-key mismatch (Phase 3), then harden the function against silent degradation (Phase 4). The verification gate is strict: total zone count must increase beyond the 61/56/59/65 baseline for at least one pair, or the fix has not worked.